         <li><strong>Sync API keys.</strong> A second switch in the same section, off by default and available only while iCloud Sync is on, keeps your eBird and OpenWeather API keys the same across your own devices. With it on, SnowRaven writes one small record into the same private container holding, for each of the two keys, the key exactly as you entered it, when it was last changed, and which device changed it (the device's name, its kind, and the same random identifier). It goes only to your own iCloud account, and only your devices that also turn the switch on receive it. Apple encrypts the record in transit and at rest; it is end-to-end encrypted only if Advanced Data Protection is turned on for your iCloud account, and without it Apple's standard iCloud protection applies, the same as for your synced files. The developer has no way to see it. Turning the switch off leaves the keys on each device in place and removes the copy from iCloud, and <strong>Remove synced keys from iCloud</strong> deletes the copy at any time without touching any device.</li>
